:name: CAN PoC step 3a: OBC and Experiment boards on one CAN bus
:description: two STM32F405 machines on CANHub busA. obc sends FLIGHT_PHASE (10 Hz) and TIME_SYNC (1 Hz), experiment receives and prints them.
:
: how to run (from the top folder, the one with firmware/ and renode/):
:   make -C firmware
:   renode renode/two_boards.resc     then type: start
:
:   +--- obc ---+               +--- experiment ---+
:   |  can1 ----+---- busA -----+---- can1         |
:   |  can2     |               |     can2         |   (can2 not connected here)
:   +-----------+               +------------------+
:
: each machine is a separate STM32F405 with its own firmware, CPU and clock.
: the hub is made at emulation level, outside both machines, so each machine
: can plug its can1 into the same hub --> that's how two chips end up on one bus
: "mach set obc" or "mach set experiment" in the monitor switches between them

: redundant/socketcan_bridge set their own $art before including this
$art?=@renode/art/two_boards.py
$obc_elf?=@firmware/build/obc.elf
$exp_elf?=@firmware/build/experiment.elf

emulation CreateCANHub "busA"

mach create "obc"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/stm32f405.repl
sysbus LoadELF $obc_elf
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08000000
connector Connect sysbus.can1 busA
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2

mach create "experiment"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/stm32f405.repl
sysbus LoadELF $exp_elf
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08000000
connector Connect sysbus.can1 busA
showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2

mach clear

include $art
